Notebook[{
Cell["Stripe-related Rule 30 rows share their entire center trace", "Title",
 CellID->874461601,ExpressionUUID->"22a1a762-10e3-861e-525e-3f4ca097ed64"],

Cell["Troy Lowry; OpenAI Codex \[Bullet] 2026-10-24", "Author",
 CellID->36768919,ExpressionUUID->"4da796ef-9f57-a4bf-7b5c-0fc91ae30e85"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "For arbitrary finite integer rows a,b and center index c, a common \
stripe-prefix cut preserves the entire Rule 30 center trace \
(Rule30Submission.stripe_related_same_trace). A stripe prefix, read from low \
bits to high bits, belongs to 0",
 StyleBox["(1|11)(01)", "TI"],
 "; the cut j is at most c, bit j+1 is white in both rows, and all higher \
bits agree. The relation is preserved after two steps, though one-step \
preservation fails. If the rows become stripe-related at any finite time t \
while their center observations agree at every earlier time, they were \
already related at time zero or one (stripe_meeting_is_early). Row size, \
center index and time are unbounded. A 2321-state paired-row certificate is \
connected to arbitrary word lengths, exact integer updates, packing, \
common-cut semantics and the inductive stripe grammar. This supplies a proved \
source of infinite trace ambiguity and eliminates delayed first entry as a \
separate mechanism. The comparison kit contains trace-ambiguity examples and \
the open EdgeObservable reduction; this result gives an all-size sufficient \
relation and an all-time entry constraint. Completeness for equal infinite \
traces and equivalence with a numerical normalizer remain open. No prize \
problem is solved."
}], "Abstract",
 CellID->1699946459,ExpressionUUID->"1b39f900-6440-cee7-4ac6-f16a0dfa94cd"],

Cell["The result", "Section",
 CellID->1535504786,ExpressionUUID->"75d93363-5da6-51a4-23e6-ab4d5453238e"],

Cell["\<\
Work with any finite integer rows a,b and any center index c. The moving \
integer update is\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1208482393,ExpressionUUID->"25a568a6-87a2-527f-535a-810032572145"],

Cell["    Phi(a) = a XOR ((a << 1) OR (a << 2)).", "Text",
 CellID->28909615,ExpressionUUID->"00d7f70d-8d0e-ae34-30ec-ef5724b8f51e"],

Cell["\<\
Bit zero is physically on the right. Initially bit i represents position c-i; \
at time t the center is bit c+t. The proof includes the exact local Rule 30 \
identity, with the white boundary below bit zero.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->193832008,ExpressionUUID->"2f3e8453-9762-68ea-56c5-1e1d22173a30"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Read a prefix from low bits to high bits. Call it a stripe word if it \
belongs to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"0", "*", 
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{"1", "|", "11"}], ")"}], 
   RowBox[{"(", "01", ")"}], "*"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5902d484-617f-9570-0f31-cdee100bfc5a"],
 ". Two rows are stripe-related if they are equal, or share a cut j <= c such \
that both prefixes through j are stripe words ending black, both bits j+1 are \
white, and every higher bit agrees."
}], "Text",
 CellID->684317082,ExpressionUUID->"56e0e12c-de7d-6135-7e9f-f889db08301f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The first theorem, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"stripe_related", "_same", "_trace"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5708d032-2150-04f2-7d37-ca7c50e56ed8"],
 ", says that related rows have the same center observation at every time. \
The second, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"stripe_meeting", "_is", "_early"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3b7807e8-9504-b25a-6907-9eb21cb600a0"],
 ", says: if the relation holds at time t and all preceding center \
observations agree, then it held at time zero or one. The third, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"stripe_related", "_preserves", "_two"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "166f8969-5e31-e8e5-3e14-21335bc5bacf"],
 ", gives preservation after two steps. All row sizes, center indices and \
finite times are quantified without bounds."
}], "Text",
 CellID->528485616,ExpressionUUID->"234f1fb7-07c6-bba9-5174-96f1b27009f3"],

Cell["\<\
The converse is open. Equal infinite traces have not been proved to enter \
this relation. The theorem does not establish EdgeObservable or solve any \
Rule 30 Prize problem.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1392207227,ExpressionUUID->"6ee45b93-a0df-d1f6-169c-52dcd16ba3dc"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"ArrayPlot", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"CellularAutomaton", "[", 
    RowBox[{"30", ",", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
