}, Open  ]],

Cell["\<\
The essential semantic bridges identify the tail grammar, the run of the \
actual integer bit stream, and the parser's whole-row relation. Their types \
make explicit what connects the finite certificate to the final theorem.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1657269721,ExpressionUUID->"2c76c797-c249-79ca-540d-ded0f7fc4b10"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Association", "@", 
  RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"name", "->", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"rule30Submission", "[", "name", "]"}], "[", "\"\<TypeForm\>\"",
       "]"}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"name", ",", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<Rule30Submission.tailRun_accept_iff\>\"", ",", "\n", 
        "   ", "\"\<Rule30Submission.actualInput_run\>\"", 
        ",", "\"\<Rule30Submission.relationRun_full_iff\>\""}], "}"}]}], 
     "}"}]}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[7]:= ",
 CellID->2048061839,ExpressionUUID->"35077f55-9291-6519-633d-771f27244c63"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"\[LeftAssociation]", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"\<\"Rule30Submission.tailRun_accept_iff\"\>", 
    "\[Rule]", "\<\"\[ForAll] (a n : Nat),\\n  Rule30Submission.tailRun a n = \
1 \[Or] Rule30Submission.tailRun a n = 3 \[LeftRightArrow]\\n    \
Rule30Submission.StripeWord (Rule30Submission.rowBits a n)\"\>"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"\<\"Rule30Submission.actualInput_run\"\>", 
    "\[Rule]", "\<\"\[ForAll] (a b c n : Nat),\\n  a.testBit c = b.testBit c \
\[RightArrow]\\n    (Rule30Submission.Phi a).testBit (c + 1) = \
(Rule30Submission.Phi b).testBit (c + 1) \[RightArrow]\\n      \
Rule30Submission.initialView.run (Rule30Submission.actualInput a b c n) =\\n  \
      some (Rule30Submission.actualView a b c n)\"\>"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"\<\"Rule30Submission.relationRun_full_iff\"\>", 
    "\[Rule]", "\<\"\[ForAll] (a b c n : Nat),\\n  Rule30Submission.ZerosFrom \
a n \[RightArrow]\\n    Rule30Submission.ZerosFrom b n \[RightArrow]\\n      \
c + 1 < n \[RightArrow]\\n        (Rule30Submission.relAccept \
(Rule30Submission.relationRun a b c n) = true \[LeftRightArrow] \
Rule30Submission.RowRelated a b c)\"\>"}]}], 
  "\[RightAssociation]"}]], "Output",
 CellLabel->"Out[7]= ",
 CellID->1680809496,ExpressionUUID->"4ebf3687-f906-130d-7644-afe0f8b37e57"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["What remains open", "Section",
 CellID->496109794,ExpressionUUID->"65de4a87-3471-cd9f-13e6-63e1bd0597e5"],

Cell["\<\
Equal infinite center traces have not been proved to imply stripe relation at \
time zero or one. The absence of delayed first meetings cannot supply that \
missing existence statement. The relation is proved sufficient for trace \
equality; it has not been proved necessary.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->108435171,ExpressionUUID->"7bedd9bd-1d84-ddaa-2992-d0e79436a7f0"],

Cell["\<\
The historical numerical normalizer agrees with this relation in finite \
controls, but their equivalence has not been formalized. No fixed finite \
recovery horizon is claimed. Distinct rows can agree for long finite times. \
The full prize question concerns every possible eventual period and transient \
of the seed's center column; this essay excludes none of them.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->829388421,ExpressionUUID->"4c37f35a-e1a6-07fe-75cc-eb0790536dc4"],

Cell["\<\
The comparison kit already has finite trace-ambiguity examples and the open \
EdgeObservable reduction to Problem 1. This contribution adds a precise \
all-size relation with whole-trace preservation, two-step stability and an \
all-time entry constraint. It supplies reusable catalog theorems, rather than \
another bounded period or word exclusion.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->203008389,ExpressionUUID->"02f88238-86c8-66df-3287-2462337d4c25"],

